[Applause]  these actors and actresses clearly  understood the assignment when it came  to creating the perfect voice for these  iconic characters  from unusual inspiration replicating  accents or sound engineering  we all know that tom hardy plays eddie  brock in the venom films and that it is  his voice behind the symbiotic venom but  what fans may not know is that it's more  than just hardy behind the voice of the  anti-hero hardy claims that the voice he  made for venom was a combination of  redman busta rhymes and james brown  that's where the sound department came  in they worked relentlessly to trigger  the voice i'd have to lay down the  vocals for venom in the morning and then  play eddie opposite in my earpiece the  late voice actor brad venable also  contributed to the voice of venom in the  first film  gollum is easily one of the most iconic  characters in the entire lord of the  rings franchise and it was his work as  the demented golem that made him a go-to  actor for characters that required  motion capture even from interviews  circus typically speaks with a lot of  elegance which makes his golem voice all  the more surprising circus found  inspiration for the voice in his own  home they basically impersonate my cat  particularly circus based the voice  around how his cat would hack up  any  hairballs  many were surprised when it was  announced that american actress kristen  stewart would play the highly coveted  role of princess diana in the film  spencer stewart ended up working with  the same dialect coach that the crown  star emma coren worked with when she  played diana in the fourth season of the  crown the accent is intimidating as all  hell because people know that voice and  it's so so distinct in particular  stewart ended up wowing critics with her  diana voice which likely lifted a giant  burden of stress off her shoulders well  they killed me do you think  there was quite a bit of hype  surrounding margot robbie when she was  cast as the fan favorite dc character  harley quinn in suicide squad she's got  a very high pitch voice which for the  light-hearted stuff the crazy stuff  works really well but when it's a pretty  raw emotional scene you lose the gravity  when you're speaking in such a high  voice robbie's voice drew inspiration  from multiple places combining a  brooklyn tinge with lorraine bronco's  performance in goodfellas and lastly  harley's voice in batman the animated  series  i never said that  to create his batman voice robert  pattinson didn't necessarily look at the  work of the other batman for inspiration  but instead he drew inspiration from his  the lighthouse co-star willem dafoe who  used a pirate-like accent willem's voice  in the lighthouse was quite inspiring  for it to be honest it is pretty similar  the voice i'm gonna do to willems i'm  vengeance  while johnny depp's interpretation of  willy wonka in charlie and the chocolate  factory may be polarizing to both fans  of depp as well as fans of gene wilder  there's no doubt that dapp definitely  knew what he was doing depp's wonka  voice came to him while he was playing  with his then six-year-old daughter lily  rose depp would often practice different  voices while playing with barbies with  his young daughter and often times his  daughter would tell him to stop then we  were playing one day and i started to  use my wonka voice and she kind of lit  up a bit like where's that coming from  and i thought all right i think i'm on  the right track here  i never expected to have so much income  thor ragnarok presented a new  opportunity while playing the hulk for  actor mark ruffalo while in previous  live-action incarnations lou ferrigno  provided his vocals to the hulk ruffalo  for the first time had to do a voice for  the hulk i hulk like fire the sound  technicians would later on make  ruffalo's hulk voice sound a bit more  monstrous ruffalo still wanted to give  credit to his predecessor though that's  who i watched playing the hulk growing  up it's definitely a nod to you lou you  influenced that  dog  christian bale's growling and gravelly  batman voice in the dark knight trilogy  has since become synonymous with the  character the voice came to bail almost  by coincidence during his audition for  the role he had to wear vel kilmer's bat  suit from batman forever which initially  made him feel ridiculous but then gave  him an idea if you look at the history  of the guy and the pain he went through  i went i can't do this in a normal voice  i have to become a beast in order to  sell this to myself  when bale showed off his voice to his  wife hoping to impress her she laughed  suggesting that the audition was a  failure luckily it wasn't and the rest  was history you made a serious mistake  rami malek had a lot of weight on his  shoulders when stepping into the role of  late queen frontman freddie mercury in  bohemian rhapsody mercury had such a  distinct singing voice that it was  obvious malik regardless of how talented  of an actor he is couldn't pull off the  voice alone  malik's mercury singing voice was  actually a mix of his own mercury's  vocals and mark martel who is known for  his covers of classic queen songs this  ultimately paid off in the end as malik  went on to win best actor at the oscars  for the role yes of course  tom hardy's interpretation of the  classic batman villain bane in the dark  knight rises is quite different from how  he's portrayed in the comics which meant  that hardy had to create a new kind of  voice for the villain because of the  villain's latino origins artie looked  into famous latin figures and stumbled  across bartley gorman a bare-knuckle  fighter who was known as the king of the  gypsies hardy showed director  christopher nolan and said that either  they do a typical monotone villain voice  or try out the accent even if they end  up regretting it nolan ultimately agreed  to let hardy try out the accent and it  was a success  gotham is yours  until recently most associated daniel  craig with the british suave he pulls  off while playing bond but with his role  as benoit blanc in knives out fans saw a  whole different side of craig as he  spoke in a thick southern accent the  idea of having a southern accent came to  craig while reading the script after  talking to director ryan johnson for  inspiration for the voice craig looked  at civil war historian shelby foote  whose voice craig heard in a ken burns  documentary we were talking about oh we  want it to be sonorous and honey we  didn't want it to be twangy and annoying  so shelby foot came to mind  a donut hole in a donuts hole lupita  nyong'o gave a powerhouse duel  performance in jordan peels us and  audiences were taken aback by the voice  she used when portraying red the  supposed tethered version of her  character i was inspired by the  condition spasmodic dysphonia which is a  condition that comes about from trauma  sometimes emotional sometimes physical  it creates this spasming in your vocal  cords that leads to an irregular flow of  air he had to eat rabbit  and bloody  samuel l jackson's villainous valentine  in kingsman the secret service notably  has a lisp something we don't really see  from jackson i did the lisp because  people tend to dismiss people who have  defects in interesting sorts of ways and  especially speech defects jackson was  not only inspired by the lisp he had in  his childhood but also from tv host  jonathan ross who ironically is the  husband of the film's screenwriter jane  goldman you know what this is like kate  winslet impressed audiences with her  accurate eastern pennsylvanian accent  when playing mareshian in mayor of east  town it is absolutely up there amongst  the top two hardest dialects i've ever  done winslet said that she struggled the  most with getting the o's right as well  as how the people of eastern  pennsylvania often smoosh their words  together so it's not like a voice that  you hear the actor doing it just  evaporates everyone's having dinner over  there because he's a big cook all of a  sudden and no one's coming to my  ceremony is that it  sercia ronan is one of the most gifted  young actresses in hollywood and her  title role in greta gerwig's lady bird  is perhaps one of her most beloved roles  ronan struggled a bit with nailing down  her character's sacramento accent but  after guidance from gerwig ronan was  able to get it down it's a lot sort of  flatter and more laid back and the fact  that it's sunnier for longer in the year  and it's warmer and things like that  that probably has an effect on how these  people sound i i like your band  with jonah ruiz even the smallest  accents can be tricky to pull off and  these actors and actresses were able to  defy the odds and give us some pretty  seamless accents  what's your favorite voice in a movie  [Music]

